# torrc.ts-hardened — hardened Tor client template for TOP SECRET transport.
# DEPLOYMENT (operator, on the hardened endpoint):
#   1. cp torrc.ts-hardened /etc/tor/tor-ts/torrc   (or %ProgramData%\Tor\torrc on Windows)
#   2. Replace EVERY __OPERATOR_*__ placeholder below with site values.
#      Unfilled placeholders are a hard FAIL: setup_tor_overlay.sh refuses
#      to mark the overlay ready while any __OPERATOR_*__ token remains.
#   3. Obtain bridge lines from bridges.torproject.org (or @GetBridgesBot)
#      over an authenticated channel; NEVER commit real bridge lines.
#   4. systemctl enable --now secure-transmit-tor.service
#
# SCOPE: client-only onion routing for the 2027 pipeline. No relay, no exit,
# no onion service. Every session additionally requires P2P_OVERLAY_ACTIVE=1
# (see transport_anonymity.require_overlay) and --anonymity tor|strict.

SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050 IsolateClientAddr IsolateSOCKSAuth
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1
SocksPolicy reject *

# No DNS leaks: remote resolution only (SOCKS5h semantics enforced client-side).
DNSPort 127.0.0.1:53530
AutomapHostsOnResolve 1

# Censorship circumvention is MANDATORY, never opportunistic.
UseBridges 1
ClientTransportPlugin obfs4 exec __OPERATOR_LYREBIRD_PATH__ -logLevel ERROR
ClientTransportPlugin webtunnel exec __OPERATOR_LYREBIRD_PATH__ -logLevel ERROR

# __OPERATOR_BRIDGE_1__  e.g.: Bridge obfs4 <IP>:<PORT> <FINGERPRINT> cert=... iat-mode=0
# __OPERATOR_BRIDGE_2__  (minimum two bridges from disjoint /16s; add more lines as issued)
Bridge __OPERATOR_BRIDGE_1__
Bridge __OPERATOR_BRIDGE_2__

# Fail-closed client posture.
AvoidDiskWrites 1
SafeLogging 1
Log notice syslog
MaxCircuitDirtiness 300
NewCircuitPeriod 120
CircuitBuildTimeout 30
ExcludeNodes __OPERATOR_EXCLUDE_NODES__
StrictNodes 1
DataDirectory __OPERATOR_TOR_DATADIR__
PidFile __OPERATOR_TOR_PIDFILE__
